[
  {
    "id": "esignet",
    "type": "oidc",
    "displayName": "eSignet (Sunbird register of record)",
    "kind": "OIDC",
    "issuerUrl": "http://injiweb-esignet:8088/v1/esignet/oidc",
    "publicIssuerUrl": "http://localhost:3005",
    "clientId": "verifiably",
    "clientAuthMethod": "private_key_jwt",
    "privateKeyPem": "-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n<<< eSignet client RSA private key — generate fresh via esignet_register_client.py, DO NOT COMMIT >>>\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n",
    "keyId": "<kid printed by esignet_register_client.py>",
    "scopes": ["openid", "profile", "email"]
  }
]
```
NOTE (hardened/loopback rebuild):
  issuerUrl       = docker-internal, container name on waltid_default (server-side
                    discovery + token POST). verifiably-go runs in a container and
                    CANNOT reach localhost:3005.
  publicIssuerUrl = browser-facing (reached via SSH tunnel). ALSO the authority used
                    for the client_assertion `aud`, because eSignet validates aud
                    against MOSIP_ESIGNET_DOMAIN_URL (=http://localhost:3005). The
                    aud-decoupling in oidc.go (setClientAuth) makes aud follow
                    publicIssuerUrl while the POST goes to issuerUrl.
```
